-- title:
--   Fontaine's submodule surjects along a Hopf algebra quotient
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative ring $\mathcal O$ in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, together with a field $k$ of characteristic $p$ that is perfect (as a ring of characteristic $p$) and an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $k$ whose structure map is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$ and $\mathcal R_1$ be commutative rings carrying Hopf algebra structures over $\mathcal O$ with cocommutative comultiplication, each free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module of rank $p^a$ for some $a$, and assume that the Cartier dual [`CartierDual k (TensorProduct 𝓞 k ℛ)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), i.e. the $k$-linear dual of $k\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$ with its convolution ring structure, is a local ring. Let $\pi\colon\mathcal R\to\mathcal R_1$ be a surjective bialgebra homomorphism over $\mathcal O$. Here [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p A`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234) denotes the direct limit over $n$, along the Verschiebung-type shift maps `wittHomShiftLE`, of the additive subgroups `wittHom k p n A` of $n$-truncated Witt vectors $x$ over $A$ satisfying $\Delta_*x=(\iota_1)_*x+(\iota_2)_*x$ for the comultiplication and the two inclusions $A\to A\otimes_k A$; for a ring homomorphism $\pi'$ out of a ring into $A$, [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p π'`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) is the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of this limit consisting of the classes of those $x\in$ `wittHom k p n A` that lie in `fontaineKer p n π'`. The assertion is: for every $z$ in [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) taken with respect to the ring homomorphism underlying $\mathcal R_1\to k\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R_1$, there exists $y$ in [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) taken with respect to $\mathcal R\to k\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$ whose image under the map of Dieudonné modules induced by the base-changed bialgebra homomorphism $\mathrm{id}_k\otimes\pi\colon k\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R\to k\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R_1$ equals $z$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the exactness of Fontaine's functor sending a finite flat commutative $p$-group scheme $G=\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal R$ over $\mathcal O$ to the finite Honda system $(L(G),M(G_k))$: along a closed immersion $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal R_1\hookrightarrow\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal R$ with unipotent special fibre, the submodule $L$ maps onto $L$. It feeds the statements about Honda systems attached to such group schemes and the construction of algebra homomorphisms compatible with Fontaine's kernel condition used in the deformation-theoretic part of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_exists_mem_fontaineHodge_map_eq_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual.lean

